00:08:26.902 --> 00:08:28.535
We've got an unbelievable database

00:08:28.535 --> 00:08:31.056
with over ten thousand
animals now recorded.

00:08:31.056 --> 00:08:32.559
So we can look at that and see which of

00:08:32.559 --> 00:08:34.149
our best breeding cows and which are the

00:08:34.149 --> 00:08:35.937
best bulls that they breed to.

00:08:35.937 --> 00:08:37.685
- What makes a cow delicious?

00:08:37.685 --> 00:08:39.630
- To be honest, a lot of love

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.381
and I know that might sound really corny

00:08:41.381 --> 00:08:44.068
but the main thing that
can affect the quality

00:08:44.068 --> 00:08:46.913
of meat is whether the cow
has been under stressed.

00:08:46.913 --> 00:08:48.782
So we actually monitor everything from

00:08:48.782 --> 00:08:51.016
prior to conception, right
through to the weening

00:08:51.016 --> 00:08:52.762
of the calf and then every other stage

00:08:52.762 --> 00:08:53.861
right through as well.

00:08:53.861 --> 00:08:55.772
You know I like the fact
that we can put flavor

00:08:55.772 --> 00:08:57.443
into beef and make it something

00:08:57.443 --> 00:08:58.590
really different and special.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:08:59.564
- Do what you love right?

00:08:59.564 --> 00:09:00.397
- And it is, I do love what I'm doing.

00:09:00.397 --> 00:09:03.519
- I gotta say truly this has
been the coolest experience

00:09:03.519 --> 00:09:06.238
- Ya, it's been great fun
having you guys here too.

00:09:06.238 --> 00:09:08.655
(soft music)

00:09:12.731 --> 00:09:14.198
- My name is Corey Costelloe

00:09:14.198 --> 00:09:15.672
I'm the head chef here
at Rockpool Bar &amp; Grill

00:09:15.672 --> 00:09:17.963
in Sydney, and today you
guys are gonna be having

00:09:17.963 --> 00:09:19.550
two of the David Blackmore Wagyu steaks.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.972
We get a lot of whole animals in

00:09:20.972 --> 00:09:22.595
and we break them down
into all the different

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:24.548
various cuts but then we
have them all aging up

00:09:24.548 --> 00:09:25.445
in a room.

00:09:25.445 --> 00:09:27.760
- What is the advantage of dry aging meat?

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.139
- The natural moisture that's in the meat

00:09:29.139 --> 00:09:31.010
when you dry age it
intensifies that moisture

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:32.761
it's like reducing a stock down

00:09:32.761 --> 00:09:34.021
and making it more flavorsome.

00:09:34.021 --> 00:09:35.607
The first steak you guys will be eating

00:09:35.607 --> 00:09:36.643
will be the Wagyu eye of chuck

00:09:36.643 --> 00:09:37.819
really, really big in flavor

00:09:37.819 --> 00:09:39.318
and we actually we never
used to serve it as a steak

00:09:39.318 --> 00:09:41.148
we used to cut it up and braise it.

00:09:41.148 --> 00:09:42.447
All the chefs would come along

00:09:42.447 --> 00:09:44.074
and cut off the first cuts of them

00:09:44.074 --> 00:09:45.452
and start eating them and
the main chef was like

00:09:45.452 --> 00:09:47.563
that's it if this is
good of all of us to eat

00:09:47.563 --> 00:09:48.742
it's good enough for the guests.

00:09:48.742 --> 00:09:49.920
So a new steak was born.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.383
Our butcher will age them anywhere between

00:09:51.383 --> 00:09:54.070
21 up to about 75 days.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.220
And we very, very lightly
sprinkle them with salt

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.115
a little bit of oil

00:09:57.115 --> 00:09:58.782
and then we cook it
over a wood fire grill.

00:09:58.782 --> 00:10:01.161
Crust it up on each side
and then just before

00:10:01.161 --> 00:10:01.994
the guests are ready to eat it we give it

00:10:01.994 --> 00:10:03.795
a little sear up again and then I slice it

00:10:03.795 --> 00:10:04.728
on a board.

00:10:04.728 --> 00:10:06.396
Certain steaks have grains
that run through them

00:10:06.396 --> 00:10:08.106
and we try to cut them
out so that the guests

00:10:08.106 --> 00:10:09.731
gets the best experience.

00:10:09.731 --> 00:10:10.991
(clapping)

00:10:10.991 --> 00:10:12.210
- That's just for our time in Australia

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.293
We saw a cow.

00:10:14.435 --> 00:10:15.268
- Sure did.

00:10:15.268 --> 00:10:18.464
(glasses clinking)

00:10:18.464 --> 00:10:19.297
- Ya, it still gets me

00:10:19.297 --> 00:10:20.130
- Still ya

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:21.923
